 "\nIf you want, I can next produce either:\n1. ",
 StyleBox["Upgrade 2",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " with spatial derivatives and tensor transport, or\n2. a ",
 StyleBox["clean package-style refactor",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of this notebook into reusable Wolfram Language function definitions."
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "/create_nb\n# Geometric Intelligence, Multiscale Field Dynamics, RHUFT, \
and Neural Networking\n\n## Final Corrected Notebook: Vector/Tensor \
Anisotropy Upgrade with Balance Laws, Operators, State Structure, and \
Function Inventory\n\nThis notebook consolidates the full corrected symbolic \
framework developed so far. It preserves the symbolic-first style, fixes the \
signed-density balance-law substitution issue, and organizes the model into a \
consistent executable structure.\n\nThe upgrade replaces scalar anisotropy \
with richer vector and tensor anisotropy representations while retaining \
scalar closures so that the field laws remain symbolically testable.\n\n---\n\
\n## 1. Reset symbols and establish assumptions\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\n  x, y, \
z, tau,\n  rho, nu, r, psi,\n  anisotropyVec, anisotropyTensor,\n  \
anisotropyVec1, anisotropyVec2, anisotropyVec3,\n  anisotropyTensor11, \
anisotropyTensor12, anisotropyTensor13,\n  anisotropyTensor21, \
anisotropyTensor22, anisotropyTensor23,\n  anisotropyTensor31, \
anisotropyTensor32, anisotropyTensor33,\n  signedDensity, centralCoherence,\n \
 anisotropyScalarFromVector, anisotropyScalarFromTensor,\n  \
anisotropyNormSquared, anisotropyTrace,\n  sourceOperator, voidOperator, \
measurementOperator, restorationOperator,\n  sourceOperatorTensor, \
voidOperatorTensor, restorationOperatorTensor,\n  anisotropyDynamics, \
dynamicSystem, dynamicRules,\n  balanceEquationSignedDensity, \
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded,\n  stationarySystem, \
stationarySystemTensor,\n  equilibriumRules, printTestResult,\n  coords1D, \
coords3D,\n  opfState, opfStateExtended,\n  opfOperators, opfScalarClosures,\n\
  opfFunctionInventory, opfPotentialFunctions,\n  test1, test2, test3, test4, \
test5, test6, test7,\n  upgradeFindings, upgradeInterpretation, \
upgradeHypotheses\n];\n\n$Assumptions = {\n  Element[{x, y, z, tau}, Reals],\n\
  rho[x, tau] >= 0,\n  nu[x, tau] >= 0,\n  r[x, tau] > 0,\n  Element[psi[x, \
tau], Reals]\n};\n\nprintTestResult[name_String, expr_] := Module[{res = \
Simplify[expr]},\n  Print[Style[name <> \":\", Bold, Blue], \" \", res];\n  \
res\n];\n\ncoords1D = {x};\ncoords3D = {x, y, z};\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \
\"Section 1 complete: symbols, assumptions, and utility functions \
initialized.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Define \
vector and tensor anisotropy fields\n\nThe anisotropy sector is upgraded from \
a scalar field to two richer representations:\n\n- vector anisotropy \
``anisotropyVec[x,tau]``\n- tensor anisotropy ``anisotropyTensor[x,tau]``\n\n\
These allow directional structure to be represented while preserving symbolic \
closure through scalar contractions.\n\n```wl\nanisotropyVec[x_, tau_] := {\n \
 anisotropyVec1[x, tau],\n  anisotropyVec2[x, tau],\n  anisotropyVec3[x, tau]\
\n};\n\nanisotropyTensor[x_, tau_] := {\n  {anisotropyTensor11[x, tau], \
anisotropyTensor12[x, tau], anisotropyTensor13[x, tau]},\n  \
{anisotropyTensor21[x, tau], anisotropyTensor22[x, tau], \
anisotropyTensor23[x, tau]},\n  {anisotropyTensor31[x, tau], \
anisotropyTensor32[x, tau], anisotropyTensor33[x, tau]}\n};\n\n\
anisotropyNormSquared[x_, tau_] := anisotropyVec[x, tau].anisotropyVec[x, \
tau];\n\nanisotropyScalarFromVector[x_, tau_] := \
Sqrt[anisotropyNormSquared[x, tau]];\n\nanisotropyTrace[x_, tau_] := \
Tr[anisotropyTensor[x, tau]];\n\nanisotropyScalarFromTensor[x_, tau_] := \
anisotropyTrace[x, tau];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 2 complete: anisotropy \
vector/tensor fields and scalar closures defined.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n\
]];\n\nColumn[{\n  anisotropyVec[x, tau],\n  anisotropyTensor[x, tau],\n  \
anisotropyNormSquared[x, tau],\n  anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau],\n  \
anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau]\n}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Define signed \
density, coherence, and equilibrium rule\n\n```wl\nsignedDensity[x_, tau_] := \
rho[x, tau] - nu[x, tau];\n\ncentralCoherence[x_, tau_] := psi[x, tau] - \
signedDensity[x, tau];\n\nequilibriumRules = {\n  psi[x, tau] -> rho[x, tau] \
- nu[x, tau]\n};\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 3 complete: signed density and \
coherence definitions retained.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
printTestResult[\n  \"Central coherence vanishes under equilibrium rule\",\n  \
centralCoherence[x, tau] /. equilibriumRules\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Define \
vector-based prototype operators\n\nThe active dynamics use the scalar \
closure\n$$a_v(x,\\tau)=\\|\\mathbf a(x,\\tau)\\|.$$\n\n```wl\n\
sourceOperator[x_, tau_] :=\n  rho[x, tau] - nu[x, tau] + \
anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau] r[x, tau];\n\nvoidOperator[x_, tau_] :=\n  \
nu[x, tau] - anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau] signedDensity[x, tau];\n\n\
measurementOperator[x_, tau_] :=\n  r[x, tau] psi[x, tau];\n\n\
restorationOperator[x_, tau_] :=\n  anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau] \
measurementOperator[x, tau];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 4 complete: \
vector-anisotropy operators defined.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
Column[{\n  sourceOperator[x, tau],\n  voidOperator[x, tau],\n  \
measurementOperator[x, tau],\n  restorationOperator[x, tau]\n}]\n```\n\n---\n\
\n## 5. Define tensor-based alternative operators\n\nThe tensor alternative \
is kept available through the scalar closure\n\
$$a_T(x,\\tau)=\\mathrm{Tr}(A(x,\\tau)).$$\n\n```wl\nsourceOperatorTensor[x_, \
tau_] :=\n  rho[x, tau] - nu[x, tau] + anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau] \
r[x, tau];\n\nvoidOperatorTensor[x_, tau_] :=\n  nu[x, tau] - \
anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau] signedDensity[x, tau];\n\n\
restorationOperatorTensor[x_, tau_] :=\n  anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau] \
measurementOperator[x, tau];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 5 complete: \
tensor-based operator alternatives defined.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
Column[{\n  sourceOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n  voidOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n  \
restorationOperatorTensor[x, tau]\n}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Define anisotropy \
evolution and the full dynamic system\n\nThe vector anisotropy is evolved \
componentwise using a prototype forcing law:\n$$\\partial_\\tau \\mathbf a = \
(\\rho-\\nu)\\,\\mathbf 1.$$\n\nThis preserves structural simplicity while \
introducing directional carriers.\n\n```wl\nanisotropyDynamics[x_, tau_] := \
Thread[\n  D[anisotropyVec[x, tau], tau] == ConstantArray[signedDensity[x, \
tau], 3]\n];\n\ndynamicSystem = Join[\n  {\n    D[rho[x, tau], tau] == \
sourceOperator[x, tau],\n    D[nu[x, tau], tau] == voidOperator[x, tau],\n    \
D[psi[x, tau], tau] == -measurementOperator[x, tau] + restorationOperator[x, \
tau],\n    D[r[x, tau], tau] == centralCoherence[x, tau]\n  },\n  \
anisotropyDynamics[x, tau]\n];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 6 complete: \
dynamic system updated to vector anisotropy.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\
\ndynamicSystem\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Correct the balance-law machinery\n\nThe \
previous substitution issue arose because equations of the form ``lhs == \
rhs`` were used with ``/.``. They must first be converted into rules ``lhs -> \
rhs``.\n\n```wl\ndynamicRules = Rule @@@ dynamicSystem;\n\n\
balanceEquationSignedDensity =\n  D[signedDensity[x, tau], tau] ==\n    \
Simplify[D[signedDensity[x, tau], tau] /. dynamicRules];\n\n\
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded =\n  D[signedDensity[x, tau], tau] ==\n  \
  Simplify[\n      Expand[\n        (D[signedDensity[x, tau], tau] /. \
dynamicRules) /. {\n          signedDensity[x, tau] -> rho[x, tau] - nu[x, \
tau]\n        }\n      ]\n    ];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 7 complete: \
signed-density balance law corrected.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
Column[{\n  balanceEquationSignedDensity,\n  \
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded\n}]\n```\n\nExpected symbolic forms:\n\n\
$$\\partial_\\tau(\\rho-\\nu)=\\rho-2\\nu+a_v r+a_v(\\rho-\\nu)$$\n\nand \
equivalently\n\n$$\\partial_\\tau(\\rho-\\nu)=(1+a_v)\\rho-(2+a_v)\\nu+a_v \
r.$$\n\n---\n\n## 8. Build stationary systems\n\nThese encode equilibrium \
constraints in the vector and tensor closures.\n\n```wl\nstationarySystem = {\
\n  sourceOperator[x, tau] == 0,\n  voidOperator[x, tau] == 0,\n  \
centralCoherence[x, tau] == 0\n};\n\nstationarySystemTensor = {\n  \
sourceOperatorTensor[x, tau] == 0,\n  voidOperatorTensor[x, tau] == 0,\n  \
centralCoherence[x, tau] == 0\n};\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 8 complete: \
stationary systems for vector and tensor closures defined.\",\n  \
Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\nColumn[{\n  stationarySystem,\n  \
stationarySystemTensor\n}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Run exact symbolic tests\n\n\
```wl\nPrint[Style[\"Running final symbolic tests...\", Darker[Green], \
Bold]];\n\ntest1 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 1: signed density definition\",\
\n  signedDensity[x, tau] == rho[x, tau] - nu[x, tau]\n];\n\ntest2 = \
printTestResult[\n  \"Test 2: coherence reduction\",\n  centralCoherence[x, \
tau] /. equilibriumRules\n];\n\ntest3 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 3: vector \
anisotropy norm-square identity\",\n  anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau]^2 == \
anisotropyNormSquared[x, tau]\n];\n\ntest4 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 4: \
restoration equals anisotropy magnitude times measurement\",\n  \
restorationOperator[x, tau] ==\n    anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau] \
measurementOperator[x, tau]\n];\n\ntest5 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 5: psi \
update factorization\",\n  Factor[-measurementOperator[x, tau] + \
restorationOperator[x, tau]]\n];\n\ntest6 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 6: \
corrected signed-density balance compact form\",\n  \
balanceEquationSignedDensity\n];\n\ntest7 = printTestResult[\n  \"Test 7: \
corrected signed-density balance expanded form\",\n  \
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Build state \
objects\n\nThe state object makes the field content explicit and \
machine-readable.\n\n```wl\nopfState[x_, tau_] := <|\n  \"rho\" -> rho[x, \
tau],\n  \"nu\" -> nu[x, tau],\n  \"anisotropyVector\" -> anisotropyVec[x, \
tau],\n  \"anisotropyTensor\" -> anisotropyTensor[x, tau],\n  \
\"anisotropyScalarFromVector\" -> anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau],\n  \
\"anisotropyScalarFromTensor\" -> anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau],\n  \
\"r\" -> r[x, tau],\n  \"psi\" -> psi[x, tau],\n  \"SignedDensity\" -> \
signedDensity[x, tau],\n  \"CentralCoherence\" -> centralCoherence[x, tau]\n\
|>;\n\nopfStateExtended[x_, tau_] := Join[\n  opfState[x, tau],\n  <|\n    \
\"MeasurementOperator\" -> measurementOperator[x, tau],\n    \
\"SourceOperatorVector\" -> sourceOperator[x, tau],\n    \"VoidOperatorVector\
\" -> voidOperator[x, tau],\n    \"RestorationOperatorVector\" -> \
restorationOperator[x, tau],\n    \"SourceOperatorTensor\" -> \
sourceOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n    \"VoidOperatorTensor\" -> \
voidOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n    \"RestorationOperatorTensor\" -> \
restorationOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n    \"SignedDensityBalanceCompact\" -> \
balanceEquationSignedDensity,\n    \"SignedDensityBalanceExpanded\" -> \
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded\n  |>\n];\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section \
10 complete: state objects built.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
opfStateExtended[x, tau]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Define grouped operator \
registries\n\nThese registries make the framework easier to inspect and \
extend.\n\n```wl\nopfScalarClosures = <|\n  \"VectorNormSquared\" -> \
anisotropyNormSquared[x, tau],\n  \"VectorMagnitude\" -> \
anisotropyScalarFromVector[x, tau],\n  \"TensorTrace\" -> \
anisotropyScalarFromTensor[x, tau]\n|>;\n\nopfOperators = <|\n  \
\"SignedDensity\" -> signedDensity[x, tau],\n  \"CentralCoherence\" -> \
centralCoherence[x, tau],\n  \"Measurement\" -> measurementOperator[x, tau],\n\
  \"SourceVector\" -> sourceOperator[x, tau],\n  \"VoidVector\" -> \
voidOperator[x, tau],\n  \"RestorationVector\" -> restorationOperator[x, \
tau],\n  \"SourceTensor\" -> sourceOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n  \"VoidTensor\" \
-> voidOperatorTensor[x, tau],\n  \"RestorationTensor\" -> \
restorationOperatorTensor[x, tau]\n|>;\n\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Section 11 \
complete: operator registries defined.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
Column[{opfScalarClosures, opfOperators}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 12. Findings and \
interpretations\n\nThese summarize what the symbolic results indicate.\n\n\
```wl\nupgradeFindings = <|\n  \"Consistency\" ->\n    \"The upgraded \
vector/tensor anisotropy structure remains algebraically consistent with the \
original signed-density and coherence bookkeeping.\",\n  \
\"DirectionalStructure\" ->\n    \"Anisotropy is no longer a scalar \
placeholder; it now carries directional structure through vector and tensor \
fields.\",\n  \"ScalarClosure\" ->\n    \"Current executable dynamics use \
scalar closures derived from the richer anisotropy carriers, preserving \
symbolic testability.\",\n  \"CoherenceThreshold\" ->\n    \"The psi equation \
factors as (-1 + anisotropyMagnitude) psi r, indicating threshold behavior: \
decay below unit anisotropy, neutrality at unit anisotropy, and growth above \
unit anisotropy.\",\n  \"BalanceLaw\" ->\n    \"The corrected signed-density \
balance law shows that anisotropy actively modulates imbalance growth through \
both direct forcing and feedback on existing signed density.\",\n  \
\"EquilibriumMeaning\" ->\n    \"Stationarity corresponds to compensated \
structured balance, not trivial zeroing of the state variables.\"\n|>;\n\n\
upgradeInterpretation = <|\n  \"MultiscaleDynamics\" ->\n    \"Signed density \
generates anisotropy, anisotropy modulates coherence persistence, coherence \
affects response, and response feeds source/void structure. This is a closed \
multiscale feedback architecture.\",\n  \"DimensionalMeaning\" ->\n    \"The \
vector and tensor anisotropy fields make direction an active part of field \
organization rather than a passive coordinate label.\",\n  \
\"CurrentLimitation\" ->\n    \"The present dynamics still use isotropic \
forcing of anisotropy components and scalarized feedback into source/void \
laws, so this is a structured prototype rather than a full anisotropic \
transport theory.\",\n  \"PathForward\" ->\n    \"A fuller dimensional field \
theory would allow the tensor anisotropy to act as an operator in spatial \
transport, coupling, and stability analysis.\"\n|>;\n\nupgradeHypotheses = {\n\
  \"Vector anisotropy is more expressive than scalar anisotropy but still \
requires a constitutive law.\",\n  \"Tensor anisotropy may ultimately replace \
the vector form in strongly directional media.\",\n  \"Scalar closures from \
vector norm or tensor trace are prototypes, not unique derivations.\",\n  \
\"Measurement may later need directional projection against anisotropy \
structure.\",\n  \"Spatial derivative operators are required for a complete \
multiscale dimensional field theory.\",\n  \"Linearization and eigenmode \
analysis are needed to identify stable resonant structures.\"\n};\n\n\
Print[Style[\n  \"Section 12 complete: findings, interpretations, and \
hypotheses summarized.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\nColumn[{\n  \
upgradeFindings,\n  upgradeInterpretation,\n  \
Dataset[AssociationThread[Range[Length[upgradeHypotheses]], \
upgradeHypotheses]]\n}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Full function inventory\n\nThis \
section lists current functions and also potential next-stage functions for \
extending the framework.\n\n```wl\nopfFunctionInventory = <|\n  \
\"CoreFields\" -> {\n    rho,\n    nu,\n    r,\n    psi,\n    anisotropyVec,\n\
    anisotropyTensor\n  },\n  \"DerivedScalars\" -> {\n    signedDensity,\n   \
 centralCoherence,\n    anisotropyNormSquared,\n    \
anisotropyScalarFromVector,\n    anisotropyTrace,\n    \
anisotropyScalarFromTensor\n  },\n  \"Operators\" -> {\n    sourceOperator,\n \
   voidOperator,\n    measurementOperator,\n    restorationOperator,\n    \
sourceOperatorTensor,\n    voidOperatorTensor,\n    restorationOperatorTensor\
\n  },\n  \"Dynamics\" -> {\n    anisotropyDynamics,\n    dynamicSystem,\n    \
dynamicRules,\n    balanceEquationSignedDensity,\n    \
balanceEquationSignedDensityExpanded,\n    stationarySystem,\n    \
stationarySystemTensor\n  },\n  \"StateAndUtilities\" -> {\n    opfState,\n   \
 opfStateExtended,\n    opfScalarClosures,\n    opfOperators,\n    \
printTestResult\n  }\n|>;\n\nopfPotentialFunctions = <|\n  \
\"GeometricExtensions\" -> {\n    anisotropyProjector,\n    \
anisotropyEigenSystem,\n    anisotropyPrincipalAxes,\n    \
anisotropyInvariantSet\n  },\n  \"SpatialOperators\" -> {\n    densityFlux,\n \
   coherenceFlux,\n    anisotropyFlux,\n    sourceDivergence,\n    \
tensorTransportOperator,\n    fieldLaplacianOperator\n  },\n  \
\"VariationalLayer\" -> {\n    layer1Action,\n    layer1LagrangianDensity,\n  \
  layer1EulerEquations,\n    layer1Residual,\n    \
layer1ScaleInvariantReduction\n  },\n  \"StabilityAndModes\" -> {\n    \
linearizedSystem,\n    stiffnessMatrix,\n    stableFrequencyModes,\n    \
undampedModes,\n    resonanceCondition\n  },\n  \"MeasurementLayer\" -> {\n   \
 measurementKernel,\n    observableProjection,\n    eigenbasisMeasurement,\n  \
  decoheredState,\n    maintenanceOperator\n  },\n  \"PipelineFunctions\" -> \
{\n    l0ToL1Map,\n    l1ToL2Map,\n    opfPipeline,\n    \
opfMeasurementPipeline,\n    opfEquilibriumSolver,\n    opfResonancePipeline\n\
  },\n  \"NeuralAndNetworkExtensions\" -> {\n    networkStateMap,\n    \
anisotropyCouplingGraph,\n    coherencePropagationKernel,\n    \
fieldAttentionOperator,\n    multiscaleNodeEmbedding\n  }\n|>;\n\n\
Print[Style[\n  \"Section 13 complete: current and potential function \
inventories defined.\",\n  Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n\n\
Column[{opfFunctionInventory, opfPotentialFunctions}]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 14. \
Optional symbolic inspection tools\n\n```wl\nDataset[opfFunctionInventory]\n\
```\n\n```wl\nDataset[opfPotentialFunctions]\n```\n\n```wl\nInformation /@ \
opfFunctionInventory[\"DerivedScalars\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 15. Final summary\n\
\nThis notebook establishes the following corrected structure:\n\n- scalar \
anisotropy has been upgraded to vector and tensor anisotropy fields\n- \
executable scalar closures preserve symbolic testability\n- the dynamic \
system is consistent and machine-readable\n- the signed-density balance law \
is corrected using rule conversion\n- stationary structure is available in \
both vector and tensor closure forms\n- the state object, operator registry, \
findings, and extension map are all explicit\n\nThe present framework \
explains multiscale dimensional field dynamics in the following prototype \
sense:\n\n- signed density acts as the core imbalance variable\n- imbalance \
drives anisotropy growth\n- anisotropy controls coherence persistence through \
a threshold law\n- coherence feeds response and measured structure\n- \
equilibrium is structured balance rather than trivial nullity\n\nThe next \
stage would be to promote anisotropy from scalarized closure to active \
geometric operator through spatial derivatives, tensor transport, variational \
equations, and resonance analysis.\n\n```wl\nPrint[Style[\n  \"Final notebook \
complete: corrected multiscale anisotropy framework assembled.\",\n  \
Darker[Green], Bold\n]];\n```\n\n/exec\nRESULT\n\
