Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "lets correctly combine this with the planck scale resolutions of math and \
even sub planckian mathematical cause or potential and the full rhuft \
frameworks with  all these correct structures involved and correctly  If you \
want, I can next do either of these:\n\n1. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["derive",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"0a1d12b7-ad43-354c-8f6c-d96525ad3aa4"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[" ",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"fe3914eb-080d-324e-af53-74d116a0037e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["the",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"07bdf67e-2dec-864f-8956-165909736c43"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[" ",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"69119754-498e-214d-a71d-34862da890b2"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["closed",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"2ce590fb-1e05-c847-82c4-5e6c858dfbd7"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[" ",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"4cde9afa-6829-5246-8d86-f021c3d0e082"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["signed",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"2214e7ad-68ff-8f42-9099-2be66fe6daaf"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["-",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"d522c60d-e874-c249-b7ac-e862bc54c745"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["density",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"341e0f3f-79cf-834f-aca8-024ac9e1cd2a"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[" ",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"a12cdd20-7c4f-264d-8e4e-0cd90f345481"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["evolution",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"d353aea4-6468-254a-a8bf-f7275ee823f2"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[" ",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"8a7fb65b-9725-f540-8f6b-884604617863"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["correctly",
   FontWeight->Bold]],ExpressionUUID->"6ca4fd1e-eb2f-b741-8c77-a07570b09230"],
 " from your ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["dynamicSystem", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "312dbe30-ea49-234b-b23d-932aaf668c8b"],
 "  Rigorous Testing and Visualization Notebook for the OPF/Neuron Scaffold\n\
This notebook turns the symbolic material in your draft into a ",
 StyleBox["testable Wolfram Language workflow",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " with: \nexplicit separation of ",
 StyleBox["proved identities",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " vs ",
 StyleBox["assumptions/hypotheses",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ",\ncorrected symbolic derivations,\nresidual-based validation,\nequilibrium \
analysis,\nlinearization and local mode extraction,\nparameterized numerical \
experiments,\nvisual diagnostics for multiscale field dynamics.\nIt does ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " claim biological or physical truth for the speculative OPF sector. It does \
provide a robust computational structure that can falsify, verify, or refine \
each proposed relation. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]},
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]}
    },
    AutoDelete->False,
    FrameStyle->Directive[
      LightDarkSwitched[
       GrayLevel[0.8], 
       GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
      AbsoluteThickness[1]],
    GridBoxDividers->{
     "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
    GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
   "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
  ShowStringCharacters->False,
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"57dc3213-1488-4947-9d1f-d66d62efb433"],
 "\n1. Purpose and interpretation\nWhat the current answers indicate\nYour \
current outputs show four different kinds of results:\n1. ",
 StyleBox["Definitions that are tautologically correct",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  \n   Example: signed density and restoration identities.\n2. ",
 StyleBox["Consistency checks under chosen substitution rules",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  \n   Example: central coherence vanishes after imposing the equilibrium \
rule.\n3. ",
 StyleBox["Prototype dynamical laws",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  \n   Example: anisotropy vector components all driven by the same signed \
density.\n4. ",
 StyleBox["A failed symbolic reduction",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  \n   The signed-density balance calculation failed because equations were \
used as replacement rules.\nSo the notebook currently demonstrates ",
 StyleBox["internal symbolic consistency of definitions",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", but not yet strong scientific validation. The next step is to \
distinguish: \nidentities,\nderived consequences,\nsolvable equilibria,\n\
stable/unstable regimes,\nmeasurable multiscale signatures.\nHow this relates \
to multiscale dimensional field dynamics\nThe notebook suggests a multiscale \
field picture because: \n",
 StyleBox["rho", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["nu", "TI"],
 " behave like competing density fields,\n",
 StyleBox["psi", "TI"],
 " acts like a coherence or alignment field,\n",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " acts like a response/restoration variable,\nanisotropy introduces \
directional structure,\nequilibrium and non-equilibrium behavior can vary \
with scale.\nIn rigorous mathematical terms, multiscale dimensional field \
dynamics means that:\n1. ",
 StyleBox["multiple state fields interact",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ",\n2. ",
 StyleBox["their coupling depends on geometry or anisotropy",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ",\n3. ",
 StyleBox["the effective dynamics change under rescaling or coarse/fine \
observation",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ",\n4. ",
 StyleBox["observable behavior is extracted through measurement maps",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".\nThis notebook implements those ideas in a form that can actually be \
tested. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]},
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]}
    },
    AutoDelete->False,
    FrameStyle->Directive[
      LightDarkSwitched[
       GrayLevel[0.8], 
       GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
      AbsoluteThickness[1]],
    GridBoxDividers->{
     "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
    GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
   "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
  ShowStringCharacters->False,
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ed428e3e-a595-a247-b7a1-a604af7808c3"],
 "\n2. Clean kernel and assumptions\n",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$Assumptions", "=", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "}"}], ",", "Reals"}], "]"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ">=", "0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"nu", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ">=", "0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"r", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ">", "0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"psi", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", "Reals"}], "]"}]}], 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->
  "e7218234-36b5-294d-bacc-d0bbe289795d"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]},
     {
      TemplateBox[{0},
       "Spacer1"]}
    },
    AutoDelete->False,
    FrameStyle->Directive[
      LightDarkSwitched[
       GrayLevel[0.8], 
       GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
      AbsoluteThickness[1]],
    GridBoxDividers->{
     "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
    GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
   "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
  ShowStringCharacters->False,
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"c8459138-50f1-f24b-ae3d-7724e5bfa511"],
 "\n3. Core fields and anisotropy structure\n",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "rho", ",", "nu", ",", "psi", ",", "r", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ",
       "anisotropyVec1", ",", "anisotropyVec2", ",", "anisotropyVec3", ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", "anisotropyTensor11", ",", 
      "anisotropyTensor12", ",", "anisotropyTensor13", ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", "anisotropyTensor21", ",", 
      "anisotropyTensor22", ",", "anisotropyTensor23", ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", "anisotropyTensor31", ",", 
      "anisotropyTensor32", ",", "anisotropyTensor33", ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", "anisotropyVec", ",", "anisotropyTensor", ",",
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", "anisotropyScalarFromVector", ",", 
      "anisotropyScalarFromTensor", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      "signedDensity", ",", "centralCoherence", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      "  ", "sourceOperator", ",", "voidOperator", ",", "measurementOperator",
       ",", "restorationOperator"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ";"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"anisotropyVec", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x_", ",", "tau_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"anisotropyVec1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"anisotropyVec2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"anisotropyVec3", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}], 
    ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"anisotropyTensor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x_", ",", "tau_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"anisotropyTensor11", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"anisotropyTensor12", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", 
